# E551 — Windows Conan OHOS 验证的双 profile 与环境文件边界
id: E551
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|zsh
phase: configuration|compilation|testing
error_signature: "'.' is not recognized|Invalid setting 'OHOS'|CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER.*not.*existing|file://.*predl_cache"
severity: 1
category: windows-ohos-cross-build-execution
match_keywords: Windows Conan, OHOS host profile, Windows build profile, conanbuild.sh, task-local launcher, file URL predownload
title: Keep OHOS host settings separate from the Windows Conan build executor
root_cause: Conan can generate POSIX conanbuild.sh and an OHOS toolchain while running on Windows. Using one OHOS profile for both contexts makes cmd.exe source a .sh file or makes CMake try a target linker as the Windows build executor; predownload file URLs can also lose the drive letter under MSYS.
affected_scope: Windows hosts running Conan cross-builds for OHOS or another target whose build profile differs from the host profile.
verification_cmd: conan profile show -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile>; run conan create through a task-local launcher and verify host/ build settings plus test_package output.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: task-local-dual-profile-overlay
rec_description: Use an isolated launcher that replaces only conan create's build profile, invoke recipe and test_package commands with argument lists and env=None on Windows, provide target compiler/sysroot fallback, and disable only the broken MSYS predownload rewrite while preserving official URLs.
rec_command: conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile> --build=missing
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: task-overlay-launcher-and-argv-cmake
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: target-side-finish
fallback_description: If the host cannot provide a faithful Windows execution overlay, run the official finish path on an authorized target worker and bind its receipts to the candidate tree.
fallback_command: finish <software> <version> built
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: target-worker
forbid_1_pattern: same.*profile.*-pr:b|hand.*create.*ci-result|file://.*Windows.*drive.*drop
forbid_1_reason: A single cross profile confuses the executor and target, and manually forged or drive-corrupted source evidence is not a valid build result.
forbid_1_consequence: Builds fail before meaningful compilation or appear to pass with the wrong linker and unverifiable source bytes.
principles: R16,R26,R29,R36
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
